{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"elf_hall","model_identifier":"elf_hall","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# elf_hall\n\nElf hall: a long, high-roofed hall of pale carved wood on marble footings, a steep shingled roof whose ends sweep upward, carved leaf boards on the gables. Neutral.\n\n- Footprint: 14 x 9 columns (224 x 144 units, 6.30 x 4.05 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -108..108, y 0..180, z -64..52 units.\n- Texture: 512 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 86, construction_0 27, construction_33 61, construction_66 82, ruined 53 (14 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- hall: 200 x 180 x 104 centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `elf_hall_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `elf_hall_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_elf_hall` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (0, 0, -72)\n"},"resolution":{"w